Contributing to Lightshade DB
============================

The full contributor guide lives in the book: docs/src/contributing.md
(build it with `mdbook build docs`). The short version:

- The tree stays green: fmt, clippy -D warnings, workspace tests,
  and scripts/matrix.sh --tests pass on every commit.
- No comments in code, ever. Explain it in the book instead.

License and relicensing
-----------------------

Lightshade DB is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). By submitting a contribution (a pull request, a
patch, or any other change intended for inclusion), you agree to two
things:

1. Your contribution is licensed to the project under those same
   MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms, and
2. you grant the project maintainer the right to relicense your
   contribution, alone or as part of the project, under any present
   or future license terms, including commercial ones, without
   further approval or compensation.

That second clause is deliberate: it keeps the project able to change
its license later (for example, toward a source-available license if
a cloud provider ever builds a business on this code without paying
for it). If you are not willing to grant that, do not contribute.

This is plain language, not legal advice. The standard license texts
in this directory are the binding terms; this file states the
project's intent for contributions on top of them.

